---
const panes = [
  { id: "a", name: "Client A" },
  { id: "b", name: "Client B" },
];
---

<section
  id="text-element-demo"
  class="demo"
  aria-labelledby="text-element-demo-title"
>
  <div class="demo-head" data-reveal="rise">
    <h2 id="text-element-demo-title">The same behavior in one custom element</h2>
    <p>
      The <code>&lt;watershed-textarea&gt;</code> component provides the
      behavior from the demo above. watershed compiles the editor from Gleam
      and registers it as a custom element. These two panes use that element
      with two documents, one shared <code>SharedText</code>, and the same
      in-memory sluice. This page contains no editor implementation. Set the
      channel through <code>el.channel&nbsp;=&nbsp;text</code>. The element
      emits edits, errors, and the local cursor as DOM events. The page passes
      each remote cursor back to the other element as data.
    </p>
    <p class="demo-hint">
      The component converts each keystroke into one minimal grapheme operation.
      A peer edit does not move your caret to an unrelated position. An IME
      composition remains valid during remote keystrokes.
      <strong>Select a few words in one pane.</strong> The other pane shows a
      named highlight. Type before the selection to see the highlight remain
      attached to the selected words. Content-bound anchors provide this
      behavior and keep the local caret in place.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="element-rig" data-reveal="rise">
    {
      panes.map((pane) => (
        <article class="pane" data-pane={pane.id} aria-label={`${pane.name} editor`}>
          <header class="pane-head">
            <h3>{pane.name}</h3>
            <span class="annot" data-count>
              0 graphemes
            </span>
          </header>
          <watershed-textarea rows="5" />
          <p class="pane-error annot" data-error role="status" />
        </article>
      ))
    }
  </div>

  <p class="controls-hint">
    This demo passes cursors between panes through a property assignment. In an
    application, send the <code>cursor</code> event payload through the presence
    channel without changes.
  </p>

  <noscript>
    <p class="demo-noscript">
      Enable JavaScript for the live demo. The browser runs the production
      watershed runtime and compiled editor component. The rest of the page
      works without JavaScript.
    </p>
  </noscript>

  <p class="demo-noscript" data-text-element-fallback hidden>
    The live demo could not start because the browser did not load the compiled
    <code>&lt;watershed-textarea&gt;</code> component and in-memory
    <code>sluice</code>. The rest of the page works without the demo.
  </p>
</section>

<script>
  try {
    const { initTextElementDemo } = await import(
      "../scripts/text-element-demo.ts"
    );
    initTextElementDemo();
  } catch (error) {
    console.error("watershed textarea element demo failed to start", error);
    const note = document.querySelector("[data-text-element-fallback]");
    if (note instanceof HTMLElement) note.hidden = false;
  }
</script>

<style>
  .demo {
    padding: var(--space-section) var(--content-pad);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }

  .demo-head {
    max-width: 68rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-h2);
    font-weight: 620;
    font-stretch: 118%;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    line-height: 1.05;
  }

  .demo-head p {
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .demo-hint {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .element-rig {
    max-width: 68rem;
    margin: var(--space-xl) auto 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-lg);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .pane {
    border: 1px solid var(--ink);
    background: var(--bg);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    padding: 0 0 var(--space-sm);
  }

  .pane-head {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    padding: var(--space-sm) var(--space-md);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }

  .pane-head h3 {
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 650;
    font-stretch: 115%;
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .pane-head .annot {
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  watershed-textarea {
    display: block;
    margin: var(--space-sm) var(--space-md) 0;
  }

  /* The element's inner textarea is shadow DOM, addressable via its part. */
  watershed-textarea::part(textarea) {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    padding: var(--space-sm);
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    border-radius: 2px;
    background: var(--bg);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    resize: vertical;
    min-height: 7rem;
    caret-color: var(--overprint);
  }

  watershed-textarea::part(textarea):focus-visible {
    outline: none;
    border-color: var(--waterline);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px var(--waterline);
  }

  .pane-error {
    margin: var(--space-2xs) var(--space-md) 0;
    min-height: 1.1em;
    color: var(--overprint-deep);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  .controls-hint {
    max-width: 68rem;
    margin: var(--space-sm) auto 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .demo-noscript {
    max-width: 68rem;
    margin: var(--space-lg) auto 0;
    color: var(--overprint-deep);
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .element-rig {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
